### Chat memory: introduce yourself, ask a question
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?message=My name is Matto, which teams are in Group A of the World Cup 2026?&
    conversationId=009

### Chat memory: follow-up question in the same conversation
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?message=What team did I just ask about?&conversationId=009

### Chat memory: a fresh conversation ID should not remember the above
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?message=What team did I just ask about?&conversationId=999

### Chat history: plain JSON transcript of conversation 009, no LLM call. Both turns above appear
### here, in order, with role and timestamp; run this again after enough further turns would have
### pushed these messages out of conversationId=009's window-limited chat memory, and the
### transcript is unaffected, since it never depended on memory.
GET http://localhost:8080/chat/009

### A conversation ID nothing has ever asked about returns an empty list, not an error.
GET http://localhost:8080/chat/999999
